{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4130924","formula":"C₆H₈N₂O₂","hill":"C6H8N2O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":8.0,"N":2.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Gaboxadol","ru":"Габоксадол"},"descriptions":{"en":"Gaboxadol, also known as 4,5,6,7-tetrahydroisoxazolo(5,4-c)pyridin-3-ol (THIP) and by its former developmental code names Lu-2-030, MK-0928, and OV101, is a GABAA receptor agonist related to muscimol which was investigated for the treatment of insomnia and other conditions like Angelman syndrome but was never marketed. At lower doses, the drug has sedative and hypnotic effects, and at higher doses, it produces hallucinogenic effects. It is taken orally.","ru":"Габоксадол (THIP) — частичный агонист рецепторов ГАМКA и антагонист рецепторов ГАМКС, который предалагался фармацевтической компанией Merck в качестве экспериментального снотворного препарата. Клинические исследования габоксадола были остановлены досрочно в марте 2007 года."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":3448,"mass":140.14,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CNCC2=C1C(=O)NO2","inchikey":"ZXRVKCBLGJOCEE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4,5,6,7-tetrahydro-[1,2]oxazolo[5,4-c]pyridin-3-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3448","atoms":18,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.897,"y":1.737,"z":-0.066,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.363,"y":-1.431,"z":0.064,"el":"O"},{"x":2.506,"y":0.217,"z":0.329,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.03,"y":0.887,"z":-0.031,"el":"N"},{"x":0.766,"y":-1.573,"z":0.05,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.197,"y":-0.454,"z":0.03,"el":"C"},{"x":2.171,"y":-1.06,"z":-0.328,"el":"C"},{"x":0.14,"y":0.83,"z":-0.031,"el":"C"},{"x":1.557,"y":1.288,"z":-0.043,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.653,"y":-0.441,"z":0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":0.787,"y":-2.012,"z":1.054,"el":"H"},{"x":0.464,"y":-2.358,"z":-0.652,"el":"H"},{"x":2.913,"y":-1.813,"z":-0.04,"el":"H"},{"x":2.2